{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792148903,"nonce":"rTpiOVre/Itueht9UAg9hLrWfpM=","title":"Class values in structural array slots are read with anonymous-object layout","message":"An explicitly typed Array\u003c{s:String}\u003e initialized with a class instance and an anonymous value crashes while reading the class element's s field. The class has an Int field before s, so the string read receives address 0x8b instead of its String. Upstream Haxe reads class/anon/changed correctly and preserves identity after the original class's field is updated.\n\nReproducer: /tmp/rayzor-sys-next/StructuralJoinProbe.hx. Define Named with before:Int=123 and s:String=\"class\", then var c=new Named(); var a:Array\u003c{s:String}\u003e=[c,{s:\"anon\"}]; trace(a[0].s); c.s=\"changed\"; trace(a[0].s).\n\nThis also blocks the mixed class/structural joins in TestType. infer.rs currently declines class-to-structure unification because their layouts differ. Fix the representation/coercion boundary before widening inference; copying field values alone would lose mutation visibility and object identity.","files":null}]}